*> Test of 29 section 4, Scheduled ticks (core/src/blockupd-29.cob; T0461): the priorities, the identity rule (type and position,
*> first schedule wins, 13.4), createTick (trigger = game time + delay, one sub-tick order per call), the per-chunk drain order
*> and the merge across chunks (13.3), the per-call limit, the tick consumer that drops a tick whose block changed, chunks
*> outside the ticking range waiting, saved ticks (pack: delay and priority value, sorted by sub-tick order; unpack: orders
*> -size to -1, positions outside the chunk dropped), copyArea and clearArea, and a handler that schedules with delay 0 (4.4).
*> Game time is CW-TICKS. Expected values come from 29 sections 4.1 to 4.4 and 13.3, 13.4, independently of the core.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-BLOCKUPD-29-4.
